WEBVTT

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:05.600
Everyone, when you're watching Deltora Quest,

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:09.400
make sure you're in a well-lit
room and sit far away from the TV!

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:24.120
You are my sun now

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:28.540
We all go through bad times

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:31.550
no matter who you are

00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:36.970
So don't go hanging your head and feeling down

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:45.690
Keep your head up until your heart's sky

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:51.070
is clear again

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:56.410
No matter where you are in this world

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:59.950
if you're crying and trembling all alone

00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:05.290
I'll search for you, I promise

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:08.960
Love will show me the way

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:16.840
The sun dreams countless times

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:23.600
Forever and always from the horizon

00:01:24.230 --> 00:01:30.940
Its shining light gives energy

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:38.320
After all, you are my sun now

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:54.800
The Japanese Deltora Quest is brought to you in English by ToranSubs

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:57.530
<i>My name is Lief.</i>

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:02.810
<i>I'm travelling with Jasmine and Barda to take back the gems that were stolen by the Shadow Lord.</i>

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:04.750
<i>And there are only two gems left!</i>

00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:10.860
<i>However, the Shadow Lord is now hunting for a boy, a man and a wild girl with a black bird.</i>

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:15.440
<i>Why am I the 'wild one', anyway?
Honestly, the Shadow Lord has no taste.</i>

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:19.340
<i>Our journey is sure to become
more perilous from now on!</i>

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:24.740
<i>Right now, we're headed to the Maze of the Beast, where the sixth gem is hidden!</i>

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:38.300
Once there was an Ol-io, Jolly-wolly Ol-io,

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:45.750
Hey! Once there was an Ol-io, Fearsome as could be!

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:46.250
I know that voice...!

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:51.000
Colly-wobble Ol-io, Jolly-wolly Ol-io-

00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:48.880
Dain...?

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:53.400
Woah there...!

00:02:54.550 --> 00:02:56.900
Ah, what a surprise.

00:02:56.900 --> 00:02:59.300
It's good to see you, Young Dain.

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:02.640
I've told you to stop calling me that, Steven!

00:03:02.890 --> 00:03:04.890
I'm not a child anymore, after all.

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:08.570
Very well, Young Dain.

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:16.150
To think that all of the villages along the River Tor are in this condition...

00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:20.120
It's not good for business when
everything's in a shambles like this.

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:23.370
Then how about I buy some
of your wares, Steven?

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:24.950
We may do so as well.

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:29.620
Yeah. Regardless, it was quite a surprise to see that you two knew each other.

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:34.630
Indeed. I'm also happy to be able to
meet Young Dain's friends here.

00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:37.420
So please, do enjoy browsing my shop.

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:41.800
Welcome to Steven and Nevets' Fine Wares!

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:43.300
Now then...!

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:59.150
"Steven and Nevets' Fine Wares,
Bought & Sold", huh...

00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:02.600
Where everything from luxurious
clothes fit for royalty,

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:06.000
to cheap yet well-made accessories can be found!

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:09.330
The one and only Steven and Nevets' Fine Wares!

00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:11.170
Maybe I should get this.

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:17.760
You're going to buy that
pendant, Young Dain?

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:20.630
What? Is it wrong for
me to buy this pendant?

00:04:20.630 --> 00:04:22.860
Of course not; there's no problem with that.

00:04:23.350 --> 00:04:27.200
But to think you're at that
age already, Young Dain...

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:29.230
Are you going to wear it, Dain?

00:04:29.680 --> 00:04:32.770
Of course not. It's a gift for someone else.

00:04:32.770 --> 00:04:33.730
A gift?

00:04:34.350 --> 00:04:36.860
So, has anything taken your fancy?

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:39.300
Let's see...

00:04:47.990 --> 00:04:49.450
I wonder what this is...?

00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:52.080
That's a bag of Premium Caramel Candy.

00:04:52.330 --> 00:04:54.170
It's a very popular item.

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:58.590
Caramel candy... Jasmine
would probably like it.

00:04:59.590 --> 00:05:00.510
I'll get this one, please.

00:05:00.510 --> 00:05:02.140
Thank you very much.

00:05:03.260 --> 00:05:05.180
I suppose I'll take this one, then.

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:09.100
You sure have a good eye, sir! Uh...

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:13.020
Although, wouldn't you say
that's a bit of a tight fit...?

00:05:13.730 --> 00:05:16.230
It's not for me. This is a gift as well.

00:05:16.690 --> 00:05:18.570
Thank you very much.

00:05:18.980 --> 00:05:21.570
Who's that for, Barda?

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:23.530
It's for you, Lief.

00:05:23.530 --> 00:05:25.320
Huh? Me?

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:27.750
It's a reward for your hard work up 'til now.

00:05:27.750 --> 00:05:28.670
Thanks...!

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:31.660
Now, I take it you're done shopping, right?

00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:39.090
Really, what an amazing carriage.

00:05:39.090 --> 00:05:40.510
It sure is.

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:42.300
I told you it's fine.

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:44.800
They're Young Dain's friends, you know?

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:49.220
Besides, Mum said that it's not good to profit off of friends, remember?

00:05:50.810 --> 00:05:52.900
What is he doing... talking to himself...?

00:05:54.060 --> 00:05:56.440
Seems to me that he's talking
with someone, though...

00:05:56.440 --> 00:06:01.280
Like I said, our profits are low because the villages around here have been ransacked by bandits.

00:06:01.280 --> 00:06:04.160
This is out of our hands, Nevets!

00:06:04.950 --> 00:06:05.900
Nevets...?

00:06:06.410 --> 00:06:07.900
Who is he talking about...?

00:06:09.580 --> 00:06:10.880
Well then everyone,

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:14.330
thank you for your business today.

00:06:14.330 --> 00:06:17.200
Where are you headed to next, Steven?

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:22.380
Well, just between you and me, I have an appointment with the fellows from the Resistance, you see...

00:06:22.380 --> 00:06:24.720
Now Young Dain, please take this.

00:06:25.880 --> 00:06:28.050
It's my parting gift.

00:06:28.050 --> 00:06:31.010
I hope it will be of help on your journey.

00:06:31.010 --> 00:06:32.560
Thanks, Steven.

00:06:33.100 --> 00:06:34.700
Wait, isn't this Queen Bee-

00:06:37.100 --> 00:06:38.900
Don't tell anyone, okay?

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:42.030
Well then gentlemen, have a safe journey!

00:06:43.900 --> 00:06:50.580
Once there was an Ol-io, Jolly-wolly Ol-io,

00:06:44.900 --> 00:06:51.580
If I remember correctly, Queen Bee Honey is only made in small quantities at that orchard in Rithmere, isn't it?

00:06:50.580 --> 00:06:58.050
Once there was an Ol-io, Fearsome as could be!

00:06:51.910 --> 00:06:54.160
So, why does Steven have some with him?

00:06:54.160 --> 00:06:56.950
Well, that's because Steven is the owner's son.

00:06:57.370 --> 00:06:58.050
Her son?!

00:06:59.330 --> 00:07:01.230
You mean, that malicious old lady?

00:07:02.670 --> 00:07:08.930
Colly-wobble Ol-io, Jolly-wolly Ol-io,

00:07:04.700 --> 00:07:08.150
Steven is a good person,
but he is a little weird, isn't he...

00:07:08.150 --> 00:07:08.970
Yeah, I suppose.

00:07:09.760 --> 00:07:12.400
Alright, let's get a move on.

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:14.890
We don't want Jasmine to
leave us behind, do we?

00:07:14.890 --> 00:07:15.500
Yeah.

00:07:14.890 --> 00:07:15.500
-Yeah.

00:07:30.570 --> 00:07:32.840
The river has grown a lot wider...

00:07:33.250 --> 00:07:37.080
That just means that we're getting
closer to the mouth of the river.

00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:39.830
And closer to Tora as well.

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:44.250
Alright! This is getting me all fired up!

00:07:44.250 --> 00:07:45.090
Let's keep moving,

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:47.090
Young Dain!

00:07:48.220 --> 00:07:51.930
Hey! Didn't I tell you to stop calling me that?!

00:08:04.480 --> 00:08:07.530
I wonder where Jasmine is right now...

00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:15.500
Well, she's likely much further downstream; she's a day ahead of us after all.

00:08:15.500 --> 00:08:19.120
But unlike us, she's all alone, isn't she...

00:08:19.910 --> 00:08:21.700
No, Kree and Filli are with her.

00:08:22.580 --> 00:08:23.770
I know that, but...

00:08:24.710 --> 00:08:28.400
Even so, she must be feeling
really lonely right now...

00:08:30.010 --> 00:08:30.860
Jasmine...

00:08:31.800 --> 00:08:33.140
Oh, right.

00:08:34.350 --> 00:08:37.100
Want some caramel candy too, Dain?

00:08:38.270 --> 00:08:39.430
Oh, he's already asleep?

00:08:41.850 --> 00:08:43.650
Premium Caramel Candy, huh...

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:49.490
This is disgusting...!

00:08:49.490 --> 00:08:51.950
That's what you get for buying
such an unfamiliar item.

00:08:53.820 --> 00:08:59.620
But Steven said that this Premium Caramel Candy is a pretty popular item, you know?

00:08:59.620 --> 00:09:01.460
But not long after that, he said...

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:04.670
<i>Well, only for certain
kinds of people, though...</i>

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:06.670
...he said in a low voice.

00:09:06.670 --> 00:09:07.850
Oh come on...!

00:09:08.800 --> 00:09:11.010
Come here, Lief.

00:09:15.300 --> 00:09:17.930
The real reason why I bought this belt was,

00:09:18.470 --> 00:09:21.640
to hide the Belt of Deltora inside it.

00:09:23.900 --> 00:09:26.550
It's not that I don't trust Dain or anything, but,

00:09:26.550 --> 00:09:28.500
it doesn't hurt to be extra careful.

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:29.300
Right.

00:09:38.910 --> 00:09:40.910
That doesn't look too bad on you.

00:09:41.160 --> 00:09:43.200
It feels a bit stiff, though...

00:10:00.520 --> 00:10:03.300
So now we have to cross this
marsh to advance, huh...

00:10:03.560 --> 00:10:05.700
This won't be easy to get through...

00:10:06.900 --> 00:10:09.100
But, we have no choice but to press on.

00:10:09.900 --> 00:10:10.940
Alright, let's go.

00:10:11.860 --> 00:10:12.570
Barda!

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:14.900
This is pretty deep!

00:10:18.160 --> 00:10:20.240
It's no good, I can't move at all!

00:10:20.450 --> 00:10:21.240
Barda!

00:10:21.830 --> 00:10:22.540
Thanks!

00:10:23.450 --> 00:10:24.120
Alright!

00:10:24.370 --> 00:10:25.830
Heave-ho!

00:10:24.370 --> 00:10:25.830
-Heave-ho!

00:10:29.630 --> 00:10:33.050
I suppose it really is impossible
to cross it after all...

00:10:40.470 --> 00:10:43.770
This mountain path is going to be
a huge detour to our destination.

00:10:44.100 --> 00:10:45.430
And to Tora as well.

00:10:45.430 --> 00:10:47.400
Should we go back and rethink our plan?

00:10:49.810 --> 00:10:51.900
Barda, Dain, look at this!

00:10:53.030 --> 00:10:55.360
'River Queen Dock'...?

00:10:56.280 --> 00:10:58.320
There's a ferry on this river?

00:10:58.320 --> 00:11:01.780
I'd say for sure that we can
use this to travel to Tora!

00:11:01.780 --> 00:11:04.580
I've never heard anything
about this service though...

00:11:04.580 --> 00:11:08.780
Regardless, a ferry would be a much easier and more enjoyable journey than walking!

00:11:09.300 --> 00:11:11.140
Let's try to catch it, Barda!

00:11:27.900 --> 00:11:29.740
This ferry sure is taking a while...

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:35.990
There's a signpost marking this dock, but there's nothing written regarding the ferry schedule.

00:11:36.940 --> 00:11:40.700
Could it be that the ferry only
comes once per week,

00:11:41.280 --> 00:11:43.790
and that it already departed yesterday...?

00:11:44.120 --> 00:11:47.500
Or perhaps, it could be that there's
only one every month,

00:11:47.500 --> 00:11:50.370
and it already departed yesterday.

00:11:51.500 --> 00:11:53.750
Could you not joke about this...?

00:11:53.750 --> 00:11:57.800
Either way, we can't afford to
wait here forever, you do realise?

00:11:58.220 --> 00:11:59.800
I know that, but...

00:12:04.930 --> 00:12:06.350
What's the matter, Lief?

00:12:06.640 --> 00:12:08.570
Hey, can you guys hear something?

00:12:12.440 --> 00:12:13.900
What is this sound?

00:12:20.610 --> 00:12:21.420
That's...!

00:12:28.790 --> 00:12:30.660
That must be the River Queen!

00:12:46.850 --> 00:12:50.550
I'm Brian, the captain of the River Queen.

00:12:50.550 --> 00:12:52.390
You got the money?

00:12:52.390 --> 00:12:53.440
Of course.

00:12:54.250 --> 00:12:55.940
So, where are you headed then?

00:12:55.940 --> 00:13:00.100
Well, myself and my eldest son
have some business on the coast.

00:13:02.360 --> 00:13:06.120
And I assume it's something you
can't speak out loud about, right?

00:13:06.120 --> 00:13:08.210
It's not really like that, though...

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:13.850
There's no need to tell me anything.
All I'm interested in is money.

00:13:13.850 --> 00:13:16.500
If you pay, then you're a customer.

00:13:16.500 --> 00:13:19.800
If you don't, I'll leave you here. It's that simple.

00:13:21.090 --> 00:13:22.260
Good, good.

00:13:22.300 --> 00:13:25.500
Oh and, my younger son
wants to get off at Tora.

00:13:26.220 --> 00:13:28.810
What?! Tora?! You mean you haven't heard?

00:13:28.810 --> 00:13:31.500
You can't get to Tora by river nowadays.

00:13:31.810 --> 00:13:33.270
Is that so...

00:13:33.270 --> 00:13:36.730
Then, please drop him off somewhere
close Tora, if possible.

00:13:37.020 --> 00:13:39.400
Aye aye. Now, get on.

00:13:40.300 --> 00:13:44.200
Oh right, I forgot to tell you guys my two rules.

00:13:44.600 --> 00:13:49.550
First, I'm letting you on my ship, but I'm not responsible for your safety.

00:13:49.550 --> 00:13:51.460
It's every man for himself.

00:13:51.750 --> 00:13:52.800
Very well.

00:13:53.560 --> 00:13:57.470
Second, I don't mind if you guys are Ols.

00:13:57.840 --> 00:13:59.590
If we're Ols...?!

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:05.150
Whether you're Ols or not, as long as you pay, you can get onto my ship.

00:14:05.150 --> 00:14:08.890
However, I won't stay quiet if you start attacking other passengers on board.

00:14:08.890 --> 00:14:13.430
I won't hesitate to throw you overboard and leave you to serve as food for the river snakes.

00:14:14.270 --> 00:14:17.490
It's alright. We're not Ols, after all.

00:14:18.600 --> 00:14:20.700
That's what all Ols say.

00:14:21.360 --> 00:14:22.570
No way...

00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:28.200
Lief...?

00:14:38.500 --> 00:14:39.900
Hey, polipan!

00:14:42.090 --> 00:14:44.210
You stole my caramel candy, didn't you?

00:14:45.940 --> 00:14:50.100
Here's another rule: this polipan is a bit
light-fingered, so be careful with your belongings.

00:15:02.230 --> 00:15:04.300
So, what exactly <i>is</i> a polipan?

00:15:04.300 --> 00:15:07.910
If I recall correctly, I saw one
of them at the Rithmere markets.

00:15:08.700 --> 00:15:11.200
Polipans are natural pickpockets...

00:15:11.200 --> 00:15:15.300
Stealing even the shirt off your back is a
simple task for them if you're not careful.

00:15:15.300 --> 00:15:16.500
What a creature...

00:15:17.370 --> 00:15:22.500
And the fact that that captain has a polipan means that he's probably no average man.

00:15:22.500 --> 00:15:25.850
Not to mention that he was accusing us of being Ols; that's going too far!

00:15:25.850 --> 00:15:27.800
Don't let it bother you too much.

00:15:27.800 --> 00:15:31.260
That captain also said the
same thing to us, you see.

00:15:31.260 --> 00:15:35.890
Nice to meet you. My name is Sandra, and this is my husband, James.

00:15:35.890 --> 00:15:36.950
Good day.

00:15:37.180 --> 00:15:39.900
We're on our honeymoon, by the way.

00:15:40.230 --> 00:15:43.700
I'm Gordon. These two are my sons,

00:15:43.700 --> 00:15:45.250
Henry and,

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:47.240
his little brother Edward.

00:15:47.370 --> 00:15:49.490
Oh my, such wonderful names!

00:15:49.490 --> 00:15:52.780
You sure are lucky to have these
two handsome young sons!

00:15:52.780 --> 00:15:53.700
Thanks...

00:15:59.700 --> 00:16:01.700
I'm Lockie the Stripe!

00:16:01.700 --> 00:16:04.630
Good day to you, Music Lovers!
I wish you good travels!

00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:24.060
As I thought, not having to walk
this distance sure feels nice...

00:16:24.060 --> 00:16:27.500
Doesn't it? It's all thanks to
me finding that sign!

00:16:27.870 --> 00:16:28.900
That's true.

00:16:30.030 --> 00:16:33.290
By the way, Barda, do you think
that there are Ols on board?

00:16:33.510 --> 00:16:34.800
I wonder...

00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:39.250
Ols always work in pairs, so...

00:16:39.250 --> 00:16:42.500
The suspicious ones are
Sandra and James, and...

00:16:42.500 --> 00:16:46.300
...those two who are still playing
cards in the back, I suppose.

00:16:46.630 --> 00:16:49.900
Ols can shapeshift into other
things too, don't forget.

00:16:49.900 --> 00:16:51.250
Yeah, that's true.

00:16:51.250 --> 00:16:55.810
Then, that 'Lockie the Stripe' and
his music box are suspicious, too.

00:16:56.200 --> 00:17:00.300
There's also that young woman and her parasol.

00:17:01.160 --> 00:17:06.360
To me she appears to be just an elegant lady from some rich family, though...

00:17:06.360 --> 00:17:07.400
Yeah.

00:17:07.400 --> 00:17:09.600
Have you forgotten about Mary and Ida?

00:17:10.500 --> 00:17:15.800
Whether cute or beautiful, they can shapeshift into that form to catch their prey off guard.

00:17:21.220 --> 00:17:25.330
Then, are you saying that lady
with the purple cloak,

00:17:25.330 --> 00:17:28.200
is actually the most suspicious
one among us here?

00:17:30.200 --> 00:17:35.800
But, with the captain's rules, don't you think we should be safe on this ship?

00:17:35.800 --> 00:17:39.870
Do you seriously think that the Ols
will obediently follow those rules, Lief?

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:42.000
I guess it won't be that simple after all, huh...

00:17:42.000 --> 00:17:45.470
Either way, we shouldn't let our guard down.

00:17:48.980 --> 00:17:49.660
Polipan!

00:17:52.200 --> 00:17:53.160
Sheesh...

00:18:03.460 --> 00:18:07.670
As I thought, things would be better if Jasmine were also here with us...

00:18:07.980 --> 00:18:09.310
You're right.

00:18:09.310 --> 00:18:14.390
Besides, they are looking for a group of three.
A group of four shouldn't catch their attention.

00:18:14.700 --> 00:18:18.390
Yeah. A group of four
shouldn't matter to them.

00:18:26.980 --> 00:18:28.100
Ow...!

00:18:28.100 --> 00:18:29.940
What did you do that for, Dain?!

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:34.650
You lowered your guard, Lief. Remember, there are river snakes in these waters.

00:18:34.800 --> 00:18:37.800
You may have lost a finger
if I hadn't pushed you.

00:18:37.800 --> 00:18:38.910
Huh?

00:18:47.420 --> 00:18:48.170
See?

00:18:48.500 --> 00:18:50.300
Grab on, Lief.

00:18:50.300 --> 00:18:51.000
Okay.

00:18:54.400 --> 00:18:55.890
Are you alright?

00:18:56.610 --> 00:18:58.640
Yeah, thanks for that, Dain.

00:19:07.950 --> 00:19:10.500
We will be lowering the
anchor here for the night.

00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:15.400
Do make yourselves comfortable
until lights out, everyone.

00:19:24.370 --> 00:19:27.300
Lief. That polipan is eyeing you again.

00:19:27.300 --> 00:19:28.420
Be careful.

00:19:28.420 --> 00:19:30.100
Right, thanks.

00:19:30.880 --> 00:19:32.200
Is something the matter?

00:19:32.540 --> 00:19:36.800
I've been getting the feeling that the lady with the purple cloak is probably an Ol.

00:19:37.340 --> 00:19:38.400
Why?

00:19:38.630 --> 00:19:42.600
I mean, she's been glancing at us
constantly all this time, you know?

00:19:43.350 --> 00:19:46.110
I've also had the same feeling about her.

00:19:46.310 --> 00:19:49.100
Well there you have it; she's probably an Ol, then.

00:19:50.270 --> 00:19:50.900
Lief!

00:19:55.100 --> 00:19:57.000
Who might you be calling an Ol?

00:19:57.360 --> 00:20:01.000
It's quite inconvenient to be
falsely accused, wouldn't you say?

00:20:02.780 --> 00:20:03.580
Jas-!

00:20:05.580 --> 00:20:08.290
So you'd best stay put and
go to sleep, gentlemen.

00:20:08.960 --> 00:20:09.960
Good night...

00:20:08.960 --> 00:20:09.960
-Good night...

00:20:09.960 --> 00:20:10.830
Good night.

00:20:14.130 --> 00:20:15.460
I didn't recognise her at all...

00:20:15.460 --> 00:20:18.400
I wonder where she got those clothes?

00:20:18.400 --> 00:20:21.100
She probably met Steven
somewhere on her way.

00:20:23.890 --> 00:20:25.760
Where are you going, Dain?

00:20:27.020 --> 00:20:28.270
I'll only be a second.

00:20:36.900 --> 00:20:39.780
Excuse me, Miss, could I have
a moment of your time?

00:20:43.130 --> 00:20:46.030
I'm glad you're alright. I was
really worried about you.

00:20:46.030 --> 00:20:50.800
Don't, Dain. We're supposed to be
strangers right now, remember?

00:20:51.710 --> 00:20:53.790
There's something I want to give you.

00:20:55.790 --> 00:20:58.010
I got this pendant as a gift for you.

00:21:00.400 --> 00:21:02.820
That looks so lovely! Thank you!

00:21:02.820 --> 00:21:04.100
Let me put it on for you.

00:21:09.300 --> 00:21:10.900
It looks good on you, Jasmine.

00:21:11.480 --> 00:21:12.780
Thank you.

00:21:13.560 --> 00:21:15.400
That Dain... not half bad.

00:21:16.300 --> 00:21:17.240
Yeah...

00:21:22.530 --> 00:21:24.540
I'm glad she likes it.

00:21:26.700 --> 00:21:29.000
Yeah... good for you...

00:21:29.380 --> 00:21:33.910
Well then everyone, it's about
time for lights out. Sweet dreams.

00:21:40.000 --> 00:21:44.760
It's pretty off-putting to hear him say that while he sleeps safely in his locked room.

00:21:44.760 --> 00:21:48.900
Well, that's what 'every man for
himself' means, after all.

00:22:22.100 --> 00:22:22.900
Barda...!

00:22:24.510 --> 00:22:25.310
I know.

00:22:25.800 --> 00:22:27.630
W-What was that?

00:22:38.660 --> 00:22:47.880
How long has it truly been, I wonder?

00:22:47.880 --> 00:22:57.810
I've been watching the moon all this time, bathing in its light

00:22:57.810 --> 00:23:05.230
As we moved closer, a goddess passed over us

00:23:05.230 --> 00:23:14.910
And just like that, my little dream was carried away

00:23:15.740 --> 00:23:20.580
I saw you when I looked to the night sky

00:23:20.540 --> 00:23:25.170
Now that I think of it, your name was written there too

00:23:25.880 --> 00:23:29.460
Above me, a shooting star

00:23:29.460 --> 00:23:32.880
fades into the distance

00:23:33.930 --> 00:23:38.560
When the moonlight starts to wane

00:23:38.560 --> 00:23:43.190
I stand under the lazy morning's light

00:23:44.150 --> 00:23:47.520
And when that same moon rises

00:23:47.520 --> 00:23:56.320
I'll start moving all over again

00:24:07.200 --> 00:24:08.220
<i>Polipan.</i>

00:24:09.320 --> 00:24:13.130
<i>A long-armed, hairy animal
that's very similar to a monkey.</i>

00:24:13.130 --> 00:24:17.300
<i>Extra caution is needed around them due to their pickpocketing tendencies.</i>

00:24:17.620 --> 00:24:19.520
<i> They also love caramel candy.</i>

00:24:20.710 --> 00:24:26.000
The ship we boarded was thrown into chaos after a group of bandits attacked, along with the appearance of Ols!

00:24:26.380 --> 00:24:30.730
I, who became separated from Barda and Dain, was trying to look for them, but...!

00:24:30.940 --> 00:24:34.820
Lief's Close Call

00:24:31.600 --> 00:24:34.430
Next time, 'Lief's Close Call'.

00:24:31.610 --> 00:24:34.610
Typesetting

00:24:49.880 --> 00:24:54.800
See you next time
